##DESCRIPTION
##  Perform basic iteration on a function
##ENDDESCRIPTION

##KEYWORDS('iteration', 'fixed point')

## DBsubject('Numerical Analysis')
## DBchapter('Sequences')
## DBsection('Fixed Point Iteration')
## Date('2/3/2018')
## Author('Peter Staab')
## Institution('Fitchburg State University')

DOCUMENT();
loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'PGML.pl', 'niceTables.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');

$k = random(2,    8);
$a = random(0.25, 2.5, 0.25);
$f = Compute("$a*cos(x/$k)");

@x = (random(0, 1, 0.1));

push(@x, $f->eval(x => $x[$_])) for (0 .. 7);

$rows =
    [ [ '\(n\)', '\(x_n\)' ] ];
push(@$rows, [ "\($_\)", PGML::Format("[_]{$x[$_]}") ]) for (0 .. 5);
$tab = LayoutTable(
    $rows,
    align      => '|c|c|',
    padding => [0.5, 0.5],
    horizontalrules => 1
);

BEGIN_PGML

Iterate the function

[`` x_{n+1} = [$a]\cos\left(\frac{1}{[$k]} x_n\right)``]

For the first 5 iterations.  Start with [`x_0=[$x[0]]`].

[@ $tab @]*

END_PGML


$rows2 =
    [ [ '\(n\)', '\(x_n\)'] ];
push(@$rows2, [ "\($_\)", "\($x[$_]\)" ]) for (0 .. 5);
$tab2 = LayoutTable(
    $rows2,
    align      => '|c|c|',
    padding => [0.5, 0.5],
    horizontalrules => 1
);

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION

This is the repeated application of the function [`g(x)`] to the given initial point [`x_0 = [$x[0]]`].

[`` x_1 = g(x_0) = [$a]\cos\biggl(\frac{[$x[0]]}{[$k]}\biggr) = [$x[1]] ``]

[`` x_2 = g(x_1) = [$a]\cos\biggl(\frac{[$x[1]]}{[$k]}\biggr) = [$x[2]] ``]

Continuing this, you can create the table:

[@ $tab2 @]*

END_PGML_SOLUTION
ENDDOCUMENT();
